        <!-- 9. Ontario, Canada -->
        <div class="case-study-box" data-country="ca" data-tag="trace">
          <div>
            <div class="case-location-tag">Ottawa, Ontario | Cleanroom Compliance</div>
            <h4 class="case-study-title">Cleanroom Environment Traceability</h4>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Problem:</strong> Contamination record-keeping for multi-payload assemblies required heavy manual compliance overhead.</div>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Solution:</strong> We combined BLE personnel tracking with environmental sensors to alert when uncertified tools or staff entered bays.</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="psr-result-badge">Result: Cleanroom contamination events reduced by 40%; traceability reporting became 100% automated.</div>
            <div class="psr-lesson-text">Lesson: Automated pre-entry verification is a critical component of contamination control strategies.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 10. Quebec, Canada -->
        <div class="case-study-box" data-country="ca" data-tag="asset">
          <div>
            <div class="case-location-tag">Montreal, Quebec | Inventory Modeling</div>
            <h4 class="case-study-title">Precision Avionics Demand Modeling</h4>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Problem:</strong> Fluctuating demand for specialized avionics components led to high storage holding costs and part shortages.</div>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Solution:</strong> We linked shop-floor IoT consumption signals directly to our predictive replenishment modeling engine.</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="psr-result-badge">Result: Inventory holding costs reduced by 25%; production-stall incidents cut in half.</div>
            <div class="psr-lesson-text">Lesson: Real-time production visibility is the most reliable driver for accurate inventory planning.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 11. British Columbia, Canada -->
        <div class="case-study-box" data-country="ca" data-tag="workforce">
          <div>
            <div class="case-location-tag">Vancouver, British Columbia | Test Safety</div>
            <h4 class="case-study-title">High-Pressure Structural Test Frame Geofencing</h4>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Problem:</strong> Technician movement around high-power vibration tables and pressure test frames created safety exposure risks.</div>
            <div class="psr-item"><strong>Solution:</strong> We implemented BLE wearable safety geofences that triggered automated status indicators for the testing operators.</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="psr-result-badge">Result: Personnel exposure events eliminated; safety-related testing interruptions decreased by 30%.</div>
            <div class="psr-lesson-text">Lesson: Clear visualization of safety buffers significantly improves testing operational discipline.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

